comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T16:50:18.678Z",codex-agent,"Fix: change only wording through PmClient.update with explicit unset scope; SDK read-back must retain closed status and the new title. Keep all existing empty-title ownership/correction assertions. Class audit of native release fixtures and packed acceptance found no other repeat-closure edit; other lifecycle updates reopen first. The cross-tracker regression uses real SDK-created custom status registries and all standalone projections, without git."
  "2026-10-28T16:52:22.737Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: unchanged empty-title assertions now pass; reverting only the old repeated status=closed fixture call makes the pinned SDK refuse already-terminal before those assertions. Restored fixture plus forwarded-target regression passes 2/2, zero skips or cancellations. No guard bypass or existing test deletion."
  "2026-10-28T16:53:24.985Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification executed in a disposable checkout: pm test pmc-lifecycle-repeat-closure --run --only-last --progress --allow-untrusted-linked-tests --timeout 240. Linked command passed 2/2 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; trust_refusal=0 and assertion_failure=0. Trust opt-in was confined to the disposable checkout. Both feature and fixture claims released; neither item closed."
